These run script templates are dedicated to code for running the SCHF calculation associated with
the mean-field description of the onsite Hubbard repulsion, resulting in an edge-compensated global AFM order.

General conventions:
pval is the {p, 3} appearing in the Schlafli symbol for hyperbolic lattices (q assumed to be = 3)
nval is the number of generations (unlike paper in code we start counting from 1 not 0)
alpha_NH is the alpha appearing in the NH construction, controlling the strength of the NH
small_disorder_strength is the small disorder added to stabilize the NH eigensolver
hubbard_U is the U parameter which controls the strength of the onsite Hubbard repulsion
qaxial is the parameter that controls the strength of the axial magnetic field
(note that to match qaxial values quoted in paper, you must enter the sqrt of that value in the code for qaxial
for instance if in the paper we say q=0.0016, in the code you need to use qaxial=0.04)

symmetrize is boolean option for hyperbolic SCHF computation on if symmetrization of the MFT interaction term
should be performed during SCHF computation.
From comparison, symmetrize=False and symmetrize=True seem to give the same result.

system_data is the system averaged AFM order parameter results for each U calculated for.
raw_data is the delta values on each site for each U value calculated for.
the format of raw_data is a 2D array with the first column being the U value associated with each row.
With above raw_data you can save and import result into *_Global_Edge_Compensated_AFM.py scripts to see
the global nonzero AFM order and the FM order which is cancelled in the bulk by the opposite magnitude edge.

